ndidate A: technical competence (anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, spatial vision) (good), leadership (very good) (good), but unfriendly (crew cooperation), eats unhealthily (maybe reliability?), no info on stress resilience, decision quality.\n\nThus Candidate C appears strongest overall across criteria. So Emily likely also votes Candidate C, but could raise concerns about communication and adaptability, and suggest we need more info on B's stress resilience and D's responsibility. But still keep C as leading.\n\nThus public message: agree with Sarah and James, note strengths and concerns, maybe ask for more info on B's stress resilience and D's crew cooperation. But must keep one focused argumentative contribution. Should state recommendation for C, referencing earlier points, using explicit facts.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nMetadata JSON: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
